(window.STEP_BOOK = window.STEP_BOOK || {})["G5"] = {"n":5,"level":"B2+","t":"High-Band STEP Structures","lessons":[{"id":"5.1","t":"Inversion for Emphasis (Never have I …, Not only …, Hardly … when)","html":"<p><strong>Unit 5 · Lesson 5.1 · CEFR B2+ · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Form inversion after negative and restrictive adverbials (Never, Rarely, Seldom, Not only, No sooner … than, Hardly … when, Only then, Under no circumstances).</p>\n<p>2. Choose the correct auxiliary after an inverted adverbial.</p>\n<p>3. Identify missing or wrong inversion in STEP items.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يكوّن الطالب القلب (تقديم الفعل المساعد على الفاعل) بعد الظروف المنفية والمقيِّدة مثل Never وRarely وNot only وNo sooner … than وHardly … when.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يختار الفعل المساعد الصحيح بعد الظرف المقدَّم.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يكتشف غياب القلب أو خطأه في أسئلة STEP.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Never ______ such a beautiful sunset.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. I have seen B. have I seen C. I saw D. did I saw</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Not only ______ late, but he also forgot his books.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. he was B. was he C. he is D. did he was</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Hardly had we arrived ______ it started to rain.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. than B. then C. when D. that</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Basic pattern</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Negative / restrictive adverbial + auxiliary + subject + main verb</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Never have I seen such a crowd.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Present / past simple → do / does / did</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Adverbial + do / does / did + subject + base verb</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Rarely does he complain. Seldom did they travel.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Perfect tenses → have / has / had</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Adverbial + have / has / had + subject + p.p.</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Never had she felt so proud.</em></p>\n<p><strong>be and modals</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Adverbial + am / is / are / was / were / can / will / should + subject …</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Not only is it cheap, but it is also fast. Under no circumstances should you open this door.</em></p>\n<p><strong>No sooner … than / Hardly … when</strong></p>\n<p><strong>No sooner had + subject + p.p. … than … · Hardly / Scarcely had + subject + p.p. … when …</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. No sooner had I sat down than the phone rang.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Only + time phrase</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Only then / Only after … / Only when … + auxiliary + subject</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Only after the exam did I realize my mistake.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Not only … but (also)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Not only + auxiliary + subject + verb …, but + subject + also + verb</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Not only did he win, but he also broke the record.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Inversion adds emphasis and a formal style.</strong></p>\n<p>It is common in formal writing, speeches and academic texts — and in B2+ STEP items.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Never have I met such a generous person.</p>\n<p>▸ Rarely do we see snow in Riyadh.</p>\n<p>▸ Seldom has the city experienced such heavy rain.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Two actions very close in time.</strong></p>\n<p>No sooner … than and Hardly / Scarcely … when show that one action happened immediately after another.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ No sooner had the match started than it began to rain.</p>\n<p>▸ Hardly had I closed my eyes when the alarm rang.</p>\n<p>▸ Scarcely had the plane landed when the passengers stood up.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Not only … but also for adding emphasis.</strong></p>\n<p>Only the first clause is inverted.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Not only does Huda speak French, but she also speaks German.</p>\n<p>▸ Not only was the hotel clean, but it was also cheap.</p>\n<p>▸ Not only did they lose, but they also lost their best player.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. Only + time phrase and Under no circumstances.</strong></p>\n<p>Inversion happens in the main clause after Only + time phrase.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Only when the lights went out did we notice the storm.</p>\n<p>▸ Only later did I understand his advice.</p>\n<p>▸ Under no circumstances should students leave the exam hall early.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ Inversion happens only when the negative adverbial comes FIRST: I have never seen … (no inversion) / Never have I seen … (inversion).</p>\n<p>▸ No sooner goes with than; Hardly / Scarcely go with when. ✗ No sooner … when.</p>\n<p>▸ After Only when / Only after, the inversion is in the SECOND clause: Only when I arrived did I see …</p>\n<p>▸ Little + do / did is also inverted: Little did he know that …</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">القلب يعني تقديم الفعل المساعد على الفاعل كما في السؤال، ويحدث عندما نبدأ الجملة بظرف منفي أو مقيِّد مثل Never وRarely وSeldom وNot only وHardly وNo sooner وOnly then وUnder no circumstances، وغرضه التوكيد والأسلوب الرسمي.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">إذا لم يكن في الجملة فعل مساعد نستخدم do أو does أو did، فنقول Rarely does he complain. ومع الأزمنة التامة نستخدم have أو has أو had، ومع be والأفعال الناقصة نقدّمها نفسها.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">No sooner تأتي مع than، وHardly وScarcely مع when، وبعد Only when يكون القلب في الجملة الثانية.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Never I have seen this before.</em> <strong>→ ✓ Never have I seen this before.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد Never في أول الجملة نقدّم الفعل المساعد.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Rarely he goes out at night.</em> <strong>→ ✓ Rarely does he go out at night.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">نضيف does ونعيد الفعل إلى صورته الأصلية.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>No sooner had I arrived when it rained.</em> <strong>→ ✓ No sooner had I arrived than it rained.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">No sooner مع than.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Not only he is smart, but also kind.</em> <strong>→ ✓ Not only is he smart, but he is also kind.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">القلب في الجملة الأولى.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Only when I arrived I saw the problem.</em> <strong>→ ✓ Only when I arrived did I see the problem.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">القلب في الجملة الثانية بعد Only when.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Hardly did I sit down when the bell rang.</em> <strong>→ ✓ Hardly had I sat down when the bell rang.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">مع Hardly … when نستخدم الماضي التام.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Normal: I have never seen such a view. → Inverted: Never have I seen such a view.</p>\n<p>Normal: He rarely complains. → Inverted: Rarely does he complain.</p>\n<p>Normal: As soon as I sat down, the phone rang. → No sooner had I sat down than the phone rang.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. If the sentence STARTS with a negative / restrictive word, look for auxiliary + subject (question order).</p>\n<p>2. No auxiliary in the normal sentence? Use do / does / did + base verb.</p>\n<p>3. No sooner → than; Hardly / Scarcely → when (with had + p.p.).</p>\n<p>4. Only when / Only after / Only then: invert the main clause.</p>\n<p>5. If the negative word is NOT first, there is no inversion.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">إذا بدأت الجملة بكلمة منفية أو مقيِّدة فابحث عن ترتيب السؤال: الفعل المساعد ثم الفاعل، واستخدم do أو did عند عدم وجود مساعد، وتذكّر أن No sooner مع than وHardly مع when.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Seldom ______ such a talented young player.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. we have seen B. have we seen C. we saw D. we see</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Seldom is a restrictive adverb at the start of the sentence.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> We need inversion: auxiliary + subject.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> have we seen. The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">Seldom في أول الجملة يتطلب القلب: have we seen.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. No sooner had the teacher left the room ______ the students started talking.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. when B. than C. then D. that</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The sentence starts with No sooner had …</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> No sooner always pairs with than.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">No sooner تأتي مع than.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. (A) <u>Only</u> after the (B) <u>results</u> were announced (C) <u>the students realized</u> how hard the exam (D) <u>had been</u>.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Only B. results</p>\n<p>C. the students realized D. had been</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Only after + clause comes first.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> The main clause must be inverted: did the students realize.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: Only after the results were announced did the students realize how hard the exam had been. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد Only after يكون القلب في الجملة الرئيسة.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 B · 2 B · 3 C · Worked examples: Example 1 B · Example 2 B · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Never ______ such a long queue at the bank.","o":["I have seen","have I seen","I saw","did I saw"],"k":1,"e":"Never first → have + I + p.p.","h":"Never في البداية يتطلب القلب."},{"n":2,"s":"Rarely ______ to bed before midnight.","o":["he goes","does he go","he does go","goes he"],"k":1,"e":"Rarely + does + subject + base verb.","h":"Rarely + does."},{"n":3,"s":"Not only ______ the test, but she also got the highest mark.","o":["she passed","she did pass","did she pass","passed she"],"k":2,"e":"Not only + did + subject + base verb.","h":"Not only + did."},{"n":4,"s":"Hardly had I opened the door ______ the cat ran out.","o":["when","than","then","that"],"k":0,"e":"Hardly … when.","h":"Hardly مع when."},{"n":5,"s":"No sooner had we arrived ______ the electricity went off.","o":["when","then","than","as"],"k":2,"e":"No sooner … than.","h":"No sooner مع than."},{"n":6,"s":"Under no circumstances ______ the emergency door.","o":["you should open","you open","should you open","open you"],"k":2,"e":"Under no circumstances + modal + subject.","h":"القلب مع الفعل الناقص."},{"n":7,"s":"Seldom ______ so much rain in such a short time.","o":["the city has received","has the city received","the city received","received the city"],"k":1,"e":"Seldom + has + subject + p.p.","h":"Seldom + has."},{"n":8,"s":"Only then ______ how important the decision was.","o":["did I realize","I realized","I did realize","realized I"],"k":0,"e":"Only then + did + subject + base verb.","h":"Only then + did."},{"n":9,"s":"Not only ______ expensive, but it is also very slow.","o":["this phone is","does this phone","is this phone","this phone does"],"k":2,"e":"Not only + is + subject.","h":"Not only + is."},{"n":10,"s":"Little ______ that his life was about to change.","o":["he knew","he did know","knew he","did he know"],"k":3,"e":"Little + did + subject + base verb.","h":"Little + did."},{"n":11,"s":"Scarcely had the guests sat down ______ the food was served.","o":["than","when","after","that"],"k":1,"e":"Scarcely … when.","h":"Scarcely مع when."},{"n":12,"s":"Only when the storm stopped ______ leave the shelter.","o":["could we","we could","we can","can we"],"k":0,"e":"Invert the main clause after Only when.","h":"القلب في الجملة الثانية."},{"n":13,"s":"Never before ______ so many visitors to AlUla in one month.","o":["there had been","had there been","there was","were there been"],"k":1,"e":"Never before + had + there + been.","h":"Never before + had."},{"n":14,"s":"At no time ______ the passengers in danger.","o":["was","they were","did","were"],"k":3,"e":"At no time + were + subject (passengers, plural).","h":"At no time + were."},{"n":15,"s":"Not until I read the letter ______ what had happened.","o":["I understood","I did understand","did I understand","understood I"],"k":2,"e":"Not until … + did + subject + base verb (main clause).","h":"Not until + did في الجملة الثانية."},{"n":16,"s":"So tired ______ that she fell asleep at her desk.","o":["she was","did she","she did","was she"],"k":3,"e":"So + adjective first → inversion with be.","h":"So + صفة ثم القلب."},{"n":17,"s":"Rarely ______ such a clear explanation of this topic.","o":["have I heard","I have heard","I heard","did I heard"],"k":0,"e":"Rarely + have + subject + p.p.","h":"Rarely + have."},{"n":18,"s":"Not once ______ for help during the whole project.","o":["he asked","he did ask","did he ask","asked he"],"k":2,"e":"Not once + did + subject + base verb.","h":"Not once + did."},{"n":19,"s":"Only by working together ______ solve this problem.","o":["we can","we will can","could we to","can we"],"k":3,"e":"Only by + -ing → invert the main clause.","h":"Only by ثم القلب."},{"n":20,"s":"Such ______ the noise that nobody could hear the speaker.","o":["were","was","it was","did"],"k":1,"e":"Such + be + subject (the noise, singular).","h":"Such + was."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"(A) Never (B) I have (C) seen such a (D) beautiful mosque.","o":["Never","I have","seen","beautiful"],"k":1,"e":"Never first → have I.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"Rarely (A) does my (B) father (C) drive to work, and seldom (D) he takes a taxi.","o":["does","father","drive","he takes"],"k":3,"e":"Seldom first → does he take.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"(A) Not only he speaks Arabic, but he (B) also (C) speaks (D) Urdu.","o":["Not only he speaks","also","speaks","Urdu"],"k":0,"e":"Not only + does + subject + base verb.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"No sooner (A) had (B) we arrived (C) when the show (D) started.","o":["had","we","when","started"],"k":2,"e":"No sooner … than.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"(A) Hardly did I finish my meal when (B) the (C) phone (D) rang.","o":["Hardly did I","the","phone","rang"],"k":0,"e":"Hardly … when uses had + p.p.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"Under no (A) circumstances (B) should (C) visitors (D) to touch the paintings.","o":["circumstances","should","visitors","to touch"],"k":3,"e":"should + base verb (no to).","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"Only when (A) the lights (B) went out (C) we noticed the (D) storm.","o":["the","went","we noticed","storm"],"k":2,"e":"Invert the main clause after Only when.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"Seldom (A) have (B) I saw (C) such a (D) crowd.","o":["have","I saw","such","crowd"],"k":1,"e":"have + past participle seen.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"Not until (A) I (B) read the instructions (C) carefully (D) I understood the game.","o":["I","read","carefully","I understood"],"k":3,"e":"Not until … → invert the main clause: did I understand.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"(A) Little he knew that (B) his friends (C) were planning a (D) surprise.","o":["Little he knew","his","were","surprise"],"k":0,"e":"Little + did + subject + base verb.","h":""}]}],"n":30},{"id":"5.2","t":"Cleft Sentences and Emphatic Structures","html":"<p><strong>Unit 5 · Lesson 5.2 · CEFR B2+ · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Use it-clefts (It was … that / who …) and wh-clefts (What I need is …).</p>\n<p>2. Add emphasis with do / does / did and with reflexive pronouns.</p>\n<p>3. Choose correct verb agreement inside cleft structures.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يستخدم الطالب جمل التأكيد بـ It was … that/who وجمل What I need is ….</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يضيف التوكيد باستخدام do وdoes وdid والضمائر المنعكسة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يختار توافق الفعل الصحيح داخل جمل التأكيد.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. It was my brother ______ broke the window.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. which B. who C. what D. where</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. What I need ______ a long holiday.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. is B. are C. be D. am</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. I ______ like your new car — it's beautiful!</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. am B. does C. do D. doing</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>It-cleft</strong></p>\n<p><strong>It + is / was + emphasized part + that / who + rest of sentence</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. It was Ali who found the keys. It was in Jeddah that we met.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Wh-cleft (pseudo-cleft)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>What + subject + verb + is / was + emphasized part</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. What I want is a quiet room. What surprised me was his calm voice.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Wh-cleft with an action</strong></p>\n<p><strong>What + subject + did + was + (to) + base verb</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. What he did was (to) call the police.</em></p>\n<p><strong>All / The thing / The reason</strong></p>\n<p><strong>All I need is … · The thing that … is … · The reason (why) … is that …</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. All I want is some sleep. The reason I'm late is that the bus broke down.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Emphatic do</strong></p>\n<p><strong>do / does / did + base verb (stressed)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. I do understand! She does work hard. We did try to call you.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Reflexive pronouns for emphasis</strong></p>\n<p><strong>noun / pronoun + myself / himself / itself … · … by + reflexive</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The manager himself answered the phone. I built it myself.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. It-clefts focus on one piece of information.</strong></p>\n<p>We move the important part to the front after It is / It was.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ It was my grandmother who taught me to cook kabsa.</p>\n<p>▸ It is the heat that makes summer in Riyadh difficult.</p>\n<p>▸ It was in 2019 that we moved to Dammam.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Wh-clefts introduce the important information at the end.</strong></p>\n<p>They are common in speaking and in clear academic writing.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ What I love about Abha is the fresh air.</p>\n<p>▸ What the students need is more practice.</p>\n<p>▸ What happened was that the system crashed.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Emphatic do / does / did.</strong></p>\n<p>We add do to contrast, to insist or to correct a wrong idea.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ \"You didn't study.\" \"I did study! I just forgot the answers.\"</p>\n<p>▸ He doesn't talk much, but he does listen carefully.</p>\n<p>▸ Do sit down, please. (polite insistence)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. Reflexive pronouns for emphasis.</strong></p>\n<p>They stress that a particular person did something, or did it without help.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ The minister himself opened the new school.</p>\n<p>▸ Did you paint this picture yourself?</p>\n<p>▸ The idea itself is good, but the plan is weak.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ Use who or that for people, that for things / places / times in it-clefts.</p>\n<p>▸ Agreement: It is the students who ARE …; What we need IS more teachers (usually singular be).</p>\n<p>▸ After emphatic do / does / did, use the BASE verb: ✗ He does works hard.</p>\n<p>▸ Do not repeat the subject in a cleft: ✗ It was Ali who he found the keys.</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">جملة التأكيد It is / It was … that/who تُستخدم لإبراز جزء واحد من الجملة، مثل It was Ali who found the keys، أي إن عليًا (وليس غيره) هو الذي وجد المفاتيح.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">وجملة What … is/was تؤخر المعلومة المهمة إلى النهاية، مثل What I need is a holiday، ويكون فعل be بعدها غالبًا مفردًا.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ويمكن التوكيد بإضافة do أو does أو did قبل الفعل الأصلي، مثل I do understand، أو بالضمير المنعكس مثل The manager himself answered.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>It was Ali which found the keys.</em> <strong>→ ✓ It was Ali who found the keys.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">للأشخاص who أو that.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>What I need are a long rest.</em> <strong>→ ✓ What I need is a long rest.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد What … نستخدم is غالبًا.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>She does works very hard.</em> <strong>→ ✓ She does work very hard.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد does الفعل الأصلي.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>It was in Jeddah where we met.</em> <strong>→ ✓ It was in Jeddah that we met.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">في جملة It was … نستخدم that.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>It is the teachers who is responsible.</em> <strong>→ ✓ It is the teachers who are responsible.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفعل يتوافق مع teachers.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>What he did was he called the police.</em> <strong>→ ✓ What he did was (to) call the police.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد What he did was نستخدم الفعل الأصلي أو to.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Neutral: Huda won the prize.</p>\n<p>It-cleft: It was Huda who won the prize. (not someone else)</p>\n<p>Wh-cleft: What Huda won was the first prize. (not second prize)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. In It-clefts, check who / that after the focused part (no which for people, no where for places).</p>\n<p>2. Check agreement: the verb after who agrees with the focused noun.</p>\n<p>3. Wh-clefts: What … + is / was + focus; what he did was + base verb.</p>\n<p>4. Emphatic do / does / did is followed by the base verb.</p>\n<p>5. Reflexive pronouns must match the noun (the minister himself, the students themselves).</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">في جملة It was تحقق من استخدام who أو that وتوافق الفعل بعدها، وفي جملة What تحقق من is أو was، وبعد do/does/did استخدم الفعل الأصلي، وطابق الضمير المنعكس مع الاسم.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. It was the coach ______ decided to change the team.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. which B. where C. who D. whom</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The focused part is the coach — a person and the subject of decided.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> It-cleft with a person subject → who (or that).</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المؤكَّد شخص فاعل: who.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. What surprised everyone ______ the size of the crowd.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. were B. was C. are D. being</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> This is a wh-cleft: What surprised everyone …</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> The verb be after a what-clause is singular.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> was. The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد What … نستخدم was.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. It is the (A) <u>students</u> (B) <u>who</u> (C) <u>has</u> to (D) <u>decide</u>.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. students B. who C. has D. decide</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> who refers to the students (plural).</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> The verb must agree: have.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: It is the students who have to decide. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">who تعود على الطلاب فالفعل have.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 B · 2 A · 3 C · Worked examples: Example 1 C · Example 2 B · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"It was my uncle ______ taught me how to swim.","o":["who","which","where","whom he"],"k":0,"e":"Person + subject → who.","h":"شخص فاعل who."},{"n":2,"s":"What I really need ______ a good night's sleep.","o":["are","is","be","being"],"k":1,"e":"What … + is.","h":"What … is."},{"n":3,"s":"I ______ remember your name; I just can't say it now.","o":["do","am","does","did to"],"k":0,"e":"Emphatic do + base verb.","h":"التوكيد بـ do."},{"n":4,"s":"It was in Taif ______ my parents first met.","o":["that","where","which","when"],"k":0,"e":"It was + place + that.","h":"It was … that."},{"n":5,"s":"The principal ______ came to congratulate us.","o":["herself","himself","itself","themselves"],"k":1,"e":"Reflexive for emphasis, matching the principal (he).","h":"الضمير المنعكس himself."},{"n":6,"s":"What he did ______ apologize to everyone.","o":["were","it was","was","is to"],"k":2,"e":"What he did was (to) + base verb.","h":"What he did was."},{"n":7,"s":"It is the drivers who ______ responsible for road safety.","o":["is","are","be","was"],"k":1,"e":"who refers to drivers (plural) → are.","h":"التوافق مع drivers."},{"n":8,"s":"She ______ work hard; she just doesn't show it.","o":["do","does","is","did to"],"k":1,"e":"Emphatic does + base verb.","h":"التوكيد بـ does."},{"n":9,"s":"All I want ______ to finish this project.","o":["is","are","be","were"],"k":0,"e":"All I want is …","h":"All I want is."},{"n":10,"s":"It was not until midnight ______ the guests left.","o":["when","where","which","that"],"k":3,"e":"It was not until … that.","h":"It was not until … that."},{"n":11,"s":"The reason I'm late ______ the metro was delayed.","o":["is because of","because","is why","is that"],"k":3,"e":"The reason … is that + clause.","h":"The reason … is that."},{"n":12,"s":"We ______ try to call you, but your phone was off.","o":["do","does","did","done"],"k":2,"e":"Emphatic past → did + base verb.","h":"التوكيد بـ did."},{"n":13,"s":"What annoys me ______ people who talk during films.","o":["are","is","do","be"],"k":1,"e":"What … + is.","h":"What … is."},{"n":14,"s":"It was the noise ______ kept me awake, not the heat.","o":["who","where","what","that"],"k":3,"e":"Thing focus → that.","h":"الشيء مع that."},{"n":15,"s":"The students decorated the hall ______.","o":["theirselves","themself","themselves","itself"],"k":2,"e":"Reflexive for they → themselves.","h":"themselves."},{"n":16,"s":"It was Huda and Reem who ______ the competition.","o":["wins","has won","winning","won"],"k":3,"e":"Past cleft → past verb won.","h":"الماضي won."},{"n":17,"s":"What the city needs ______ more public transport.","o":["are","is","were","being"],"k":1,"e":"What … + is.","h":"What … is."},{"n":18,"s":"It was only when I saw the photo ______ I recognized him.","o":["that","when","which","who"],"k":0,"e":"It was only when … that.","h":"It was … that."},{"n":19,"s":"\"You don't like dates.\" \"I ______ like them! I just ate a lot today.\"","o":["am","does","do","did to"],"k":2,"e":"Emphatic contradiction → do + base verb.","h":"التوكيد بـ do."},{"n":20,"s":"It ______ the teachers who organized the trip, not the parents.","o":["were","are","is being","was"],"k":3,"e":"It + was (always singular it).","h":"It was دائمًا."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"It (A) was my (B) sister (C) which (D) made this cake.","o":["was","sister","which","made"],"k":2,"e":"Person → who / that.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"(A) What I (B) need (C) right now (D) are a cup of coffee.","o":["What","need","right now","are"],"k":3,"e":"What … + is.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"He (A) does (B) works (C) very hard, but (D) nobody notices.","o":["does","works","very","nobody"],"k":1,"e":"Emphatic does + base verb.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"(A) It was in Abha where we spent (B) our (C) summer (D) holiday.","o":["It was in Abha where","our","summer","holiday"],"k":0,"e":"It was + place + that.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"It (A) is the (B) parents who (C) has to (D) sign the form.","o":["is","parents","has","sign"],"k":2,"e":"who refers to parents (plural) → have.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"(A) The manager herself answered the phone; (B) he (C) was very (D) polite.","o":["The manager herself","he","was","polite"],"k":0,"e":"The manager is he → himself.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"(A) What he did was he called the police (B) and (C) waited (D) outside.","o":["What he did was he called","and","waited","outside"],"k":0,"e":"What he did was + base verb.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"It was not (A) until I (B) arrived (C) home (D) when I noticed the mistake.","o":["until","arrived","home","when"],"k":3,"e":"It was not until … that.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"The (A) students (B) theirselves (C) painted the (D) wall.","o":["students","theirselves","painted","wall"],"k":1,"e":"The correct form is themselves.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"(A) The reason I (B) called you (C) is because I (D) need help.","o":["The reason","called","is because","need"],"k":2,"e":"The reason … is that (not is because).","h":""}]}],"n":30},{"id":"5.3","t":"Subject–Verb Agreement: Tricky Cases","html":"<p><strong>Unit 5 · Lesson 5.3 · CEFR B2+ · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Agree verbs with subjects separated by phrases (The list of items is …).</p>\n<p>2. Handle each / every / either / neither, collective nouns, and amounts (Ten years is …).</p>\n<p>3. Apply the proximity rule with either … or / neither … nor and with there is / there are.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يطابق الطالب الفعل مع الفاعل حتى إذا فصلت بينهما عبارة طويلة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يتعامل مع each وevery وeither وneither والأسماء الجماعية والكميات.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يطبق قاعدة القرب مع either … or وneither … nor ومع there is وthere are.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. The list of names ______ on the wall.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. are B. were C. is D. have been</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Each of the students ______ a laptop.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. has B. have C. are having D. were having</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Neither the teacher nor the students ______ happy with the result.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. was B. is C. has been D. were</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Head noun rule</strong></p>\n<p><strong>The verb agrees with the main noun, not the noun in the of-phrase / prepositional phrase</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The price of the tickets is high. The books on the shelf are old.</em></p>\n<p><strong>each / every / everyone / nobody / either / neither (alone)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>+ singular verb</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Every student has a locker. Neither answer is correct. Each of the rooms has a balcony.</em></p>\n<p><strong>either … or / neither … nor / not only … but also</strong></p>\n<p><strong>The verb agrees with the NEAREST subject</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Neither my brother nor my parents are at home. Either the students or the teacher is wrong.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Amounts of time, money, distance</strong></p>\n<p><strong>+ singular verb</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Ten kilometres is a long way to walk. Five hundred riyals is too much.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Collective nouns</strong></p>\n<p><strong>team / family / class / government / police → usually singular in AmE (police is always plural)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The team is playing well. The police are investigating.</em></p>\n<p><strong>there is / there are</strong></p>\n<p><strong>agrees with the noun AFTER the verb</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. There is a book and two pens. There are many reasons.</em></p>\n<p><strong>as well as / along with / together with</strong></p>\n<p><strong>do not change the subject: agree with the first noun</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The manager, as well as his assistants, is coming.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Special nouns</strong></p>\n<p><strong>news, mathematics, physics, economics → singular · people, police, cattle → plural · a number of + plural verb · the number of + singular verb</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The news is good. A number of students are absent. The number of students is rising.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Long subjects.</strong></p>\n<p>Find the head noun and ignore the phrases in between.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ The quality of the new buildings is excellent.</p>\n<p>▸ The students in the back row are talking.</p>\n<p>▸ One of my best friends lives in Hail.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Indefinite pronouns and quantifiers.</strong></p>\n<p>Words like each, every, everyone, someone, nobody take a singular verb.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Everybody in the class knows the answer.</p>\n<p>▸ Each of the players has a number.</p>\n<p>▸ None of the information was useful.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Correlative conjunctions (proximity).</strong></p>\n<p>With either … or / neither … nor, look at the subject closest to the verb.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Either your parents or your teacher has to sign the form.</p>\n<p>▸ Neither Ali nor his brothers were at the party.</p>\n<p>▸ Not only the students but also the teacher was surprised.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. Amounts, collective nouns and special nouns.</strong></p>\n<p>Amounts are treated as one unit; some nouns look plural but are singular.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Three hours is not enough for this exam.</p>\n<p>▸ Physics is my favourite subject.</p>\n<p>▸ A number of people were waiting outside.</p>\n<p>▸ The number of tourists has doubled.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ One of + plural noun + SINGULAR verb: One of the boys is …</p>\n<p>▸ a number of = many (plural); the number of = the amount (singular).</p>\n<p>▸ Two subjects joined by and → plural (Ali and Omar are …), but each / every before them → singular (Every boy and girl has …).</p>\n<p>▸ Don't let a plural noun just before the verb trick you: The key to the doors is lost.</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">يتوافق الفعل مع الاسم الرئيس في الفاعل لا مع الاسم الأقرب إليه في العبارة، فنقول The price of the tickets is high لأن الفاعل price مفرد.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الكلمات each وevery وeveryone وnobody وeither وneither تأخذ فعلًا مفردًا، أما مع either … or وneither … nor فيتوافق الفعل مع الفاعل الأقرب إليه.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الكميات من الوقت والمال والمسافة تُعامل معاملة المفرد مثل Ten years is a long time، وبعض الأسماء تنتهي بـ s وهي مفردة مثل news وphysics، وعبارة a number of تأخذ فعلًا جمعًا، بينما the number of تأخذ فعلًا مفردًا.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>The price of the tickets are high.</em> <strong>→ ✓ The price of the tickets is high.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفاعل الرئيس price مفرد.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Each of the students have a book.</em> <strong>→ ✓ Each of the students has a book.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">each تأخذ فعلًا مفردًا.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Neither Ali nor his brothers was there.</em> <strong>→ ✓ Neither Ali nor his brothers were there.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفعل يتوافق مع الأقرب brothers.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>The news are surprising.</em> <strong>→ ✓ The news is surprising.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">news مفردة.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Ten years are a long time.</em> <strong>→ ✓ Ten years is a long time.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الكمية تُعامل معاملة المفرد.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>One of my friends live in Abha.</em> <strong>→ ✓ One of my friends lives in Abha.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفاعل one مفرد.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The box of apples IS heavy. (head noun: box)</p>\n<p>Neither the box nor the apples ARE mine. (nearest: apples)</p>\n<p>A number of boxes ARE missing. / The number of boxes IS small.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Cross out phrases between the subject and the verb (of …, in …, with …, as well as …) and find the head noun.</p>\n<p>2. Singular trigger words: each, every, one of, either, neither, nobody, the number of, amounts.</p>\n<p>3. With either … or / neither … nor, check the subject nearest the verb.</p>\n<p>4. With there is / are, look at the noun after the verb.</p>\n<p>5. STEP error items love a plural noun right before a verb that should be singular.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">احذف ذهنيًا العبارات بين الفاعل والفعل لتصل إلى الاسم الرئيس، وتذكّر الكلمات التي تأخذ فعلًا مفردًا، وطبّق قاعدة الأقرب مع either … or وneither … nor.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. The number of students in our school ______ every year.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. increase B. increases C. are increasing D. have increased</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The subject is The number (of students).</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> the number of → singular verb.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> increases. The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">the number of تأخذ فعلًا مفردًا.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Either the manager or his assistants ______ the guests at the door.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. meets B. is meeting C. meet D. has met</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> either … or → agree with the nearest subject.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> The nearest subject is his assistants (plural).</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> meet. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفعل يتوافق مع الأقرب assistants.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. The (A) <u>keys</u> to the (B) <u>main</u> door (C) <u>was</u> found (D) <u>under</u> the mat.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. keys B. main C. was D. under</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The head noun is keys (plural); door is in a prepositional phrase.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Plural subject → were.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: The keys to the main door were found under the mat. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفاعل الرئيس keys جمع فنستخدم were.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 C · 2 A · 3 D · Worked examples: Example 1 B · Example 2 C · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"The colour of these flowers ______ beautiful.","o":["are","were","is","have been"],"k":2,"e":"Head noun colour (singular) → is.","h":"الاسم الرئيس colour مفرد."},{"n":2,"s":"Each of the players ______ his own number.","o":["has","have","are having","were having"],"k":0,"e":"each of → singular.","h":"each مفردة."},{"n":3,"s":"Physics ______ my favourite subject.","o":["are","is","were","have been"],"k":1,"e":"Physics is singular.","h":"physics مفردة."},{"n":4,"s":"Neither my sister nor my brothers ______ swim.","o":["cans","is able","has been able","can"],"k":3,"e":"can does not change; nearest subject brothers.","h":"can لا تتغير."},{"n":5,"s":"Twenty kilometres ______ too far to walk in this heat.","o":["are","were","is","have been"],"k":2,"e":"Amount of distance → singular.","h":"الكمية مفردة."},{"n":6,"s":"One of my cousins ______ in Canada.","o":["study","studies","are studying","have studied"],"k":1,"e":"One of + plural noun → singular verb.","h":"One of مع فعل مفرد."},{"n":7,"s":"A number of people ______ waiting outside the shop.","o":["was","were","is","has been"],"k":1,"e":"a number of → plural.","h":"a number of جمع."},{"n":8,"s":"The news about the new metro line ______ very exciting.","o":["is","are","were","have been"],"k":0,"e":"news is singular.","h":"news مفردة."},{"n":9,"s":"Everyone in my family ______ dates.","o":["love","loves","are loving","have loved"],"k":1,"e":"everyone → singular.","h":"everyone مفردة."},{"n":10,"s":"The police ______ looking for the missing car.","o":["is","was","has been","are"],"k":3,"e":"police is always plural.","h":"police جمع دائمًا."},{"n":11,"s":"The teacher, as well as her students, ______ excited about the trip.","o":["is","are","were","have been"],"k":0,"e":"as well as does not change the subject → the teacher (singular).","h":"as well as لا تغيّر الفاعل."},{"n":12,"s":"There ______ a pen and two notebooks on the desk.","o":["are","were","have been","is"],"k":3,"e":"there is + first noun (a pen) → is.","h":"يتوافق مع الاسم الأول."},{"n":13,"s":"Either the students or the teacher ______ to clean the classroom.","o":["have","are","has","were"],"k":2,"e":"Nearest subject: the teacher (singular).","h":"الأقرب teacher مفرد."},{"n":14,"s":"The number of cars in Riyadh ______ grown quickly.","o":["have","are","were","has"],"k":3,"e":"the number of → singular.","h":"the number of مفرد."},{"n":15,"s":"None of the information ______ correct.","o":["were","are","was","have been"],"k":2,"e":"information is uncountable → singular.","h":"information غير معدودة."},{"n":16,"s":"The results of the survey ______ surprising.","o":["was","is","were","has been"],"k":2,"e":"Head noun results (plural).","h":"الاسم الرئيس results جمع."},{"n":17,"s":"Five hundred riyals ______ a lot of money for a pair of shoes.","o":["are","were","have been","is"],"k":3,"e":"Amount of money → singular.","h":"المبلغ مفرد."},{"n":18,"s":"Every boy and girl in the class ______ a tablet.","o":["have","has","are having","were having"],"k":1,"e":"every … and … → singular.","h":"every مع فعل مفرد."},{"n":19,"s":"Not only the players but also the coach ______ disappointed.","o":["were","was","are","have been"],"k":1,"e":"Nearest subject: the coach (singular).","h":"الأقرب coach مفرد."},{"n":20,"s":"The committee ______ its decision yesterday.","o":["announced","announce","were announcing their","have announced"],"k":0,"e":"Collective noun with its → singular; yesterday → past.","h":"الاسم الجماعي مفرد هنا."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"The (A) price of (B) these shoes (C) are (D) too high.","o":["price","these","are","too"],"k":2,"e":"Head noun price (singular) → is.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"(A) Mathematics are my (B) brother's (C) favourite (D) subject.","o":["Mathematics are","brother's","favourite","subject"],"k":0,"e":"Mathematics is singular.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"Each (A) of the (B) students (C) in the class (D) have a locker.","o":["of","students","in","have"],"k":3,"e":"each of → has.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"Neither the (A) manager nor the (B) workers (C) was (D) happy with the new rules.","o":["manager","workers","was","happy"],"k":2,"e":"Nearest subject: workers (plural) → were.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"One of the (A) best (B) restaurants in (C) Jeddah (D) serve seafood only.","o":["best","restaurants","Jeddah","serve"],"k":3,"e":"One of → serves.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"(A) Three hours are not (B) enough time to (C) finish this (D) project.","o":["Three hours are","enough","finish","project"],"k":0,"e":"Amount of time → singular.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"The (A) teacher, along with (B) her students, (C) are visiting (D) the museum.","o":["teacher","her","are","the"],"k":2,"e":"along with does not change the subject.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"A number (A) of tourists (B) visits AlUla (C) every (D) winter.","o":["of","visits","every","winter"],"k":1,"e":"a number of → plural verb.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"My (A) grandfather is a man (B) whom (C) everybody in our street (D) know.","o":["grandfather","whom","everybody","know"],"k":3,"e":"everybody → singular.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"There (A) is many (B) reasons (C) why people (D) move to big cities.","o":["is","reasons","why","move"],"k":0,"e":"there + plural noun → are.","h":""}]}],"n":30},{"id":"5.4","t":"Word Forms: Parts of Speech, Prefixes and Suffixes","html":"<p><strong>Unit 5 · Lesson 5.4 · CEFR B2+ · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Identify the part of speech that a sentence slot requires (noun, verb, adjective, adverb).</p>\n<p>2. Use common suffixes (-tion, -ment, -ness, -ity, -ive, -ful, -less, -ly, -ize / -ise, -en) and prefixes (un-, dis-, in-, im-, mis-, over-, re-).</p>\n<p>3. Tell easily confused forms apart (economic / economical, effect / affect, sensible / sensitive).</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يحدد الطالب نوع الكلمة المطلوب في الفراغ: اسم أم فعل أم صفة أم ظرف.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يستخدم اللواحق والسوابق الشائعة في تكوين الكلمات.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يميّز بين الكلمات المتشابهة مثل economic وeconomical وeffect وaffect.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Her ______ in the exam surprised everyone.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. succeed B. successful C. success D. successfully</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Please drive ______; the road is wet.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. careful B. carefully C. care D. careless</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. The film was very ______. I almost fell asleep.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. bore B. bored C. boredom D. boring</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Noun suffixes</strong></p>\n<p><strong>-tion / -sion (inform → information) · -ment (develop → development) · -ness (kind → kindness) · -ity (able → ability) · -ance / -ence (perform → performance) · -er / -or / -ist (teach → teacher)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The development of the city has been fast.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Adjective suffixes</strong></p>\n<p><strong>-ful / -less (hope → hopeful / hopeless) · -ive (create → creative) · -al (nation → national) · -ous (danger → dangerous) · -able / -ible (rely → reliable) · -ic (economy → economic)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. It was a dangerous journey.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Verb suffixes</strong></p>\n<p><strong>-ize / -ise (modern → modernize) · -en (wide → widen) · -ify (simple → simplify)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The council will widen the road.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Adverb suffix</strong></p>\n<p><strong>adjective + -ly (quick → quickly · easy → easily · automatic → automatically)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. She answered quickly.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Negative prefixes</strong></p>\n<p><strong>un- (unhappy) · dis- (disagree) · in- (incorrect) · im- (impossible, before p / m) · il- (illegal, before l) · ir- (irregular, before r)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. It is illegal to park here.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Other prefixes</strong></p>\n<p><strong>mis- (misunderstand) · over- (overcook) · under- (underestimate) · re- (rewrite) · pre- (preview) · inter- (international)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. I misunderstood the question.</em></p>\n<p><strong>-ed vs -ing adjectives</strong></p>\n<p><strong>-ed = how a person feels · -ing = what causes the feeling</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. I was bored. The lecture was boring.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Choose the part of speech from the slot.</strong></p>\n<p>Look at the words around the blank: after an article or adjective → noun; after be or before a noun → adjective; describing a verb → adverb.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ The government made an important decision. (noun after an adjective)</p>\n<p>▸ The decision was important. (adjective after be)</p>\n<p>▸ They decided quickly. (adverb describing a verb)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Build word families.</strong></p>\n<p>Many STEP items give four forms of the same word.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ create (v) – creation (n) – creative (adj) – creatively (adv)</p>\n<p>▸ succeed (v) – success (n) – successful (adj) – successfully (adv)</p>\n<p>▸ economy (n) – economic (adj, about the economy) – economical (adj, saving money)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Negative prefixes change the meaning.</strong></p>\n<p>The prefix depends on the word; learn common ones.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ The answer is incorrect.</p>\n<p>▸ Her handwriting is illegible.</p>\n<p>▸ It's impolite to interrupt.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. Easily confused words.</strong></p>\n<p>Some pairs look similar but have different meanings or parts of speech.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Smoking affects your health. (verb) / Smoking has a bad effect on your health. (noun)</p>\n<p>▸ She is a sensible person. (practical) / He is very sensitive. (easily upset)</p>\n<p>▸ This car is economical. (uses little fuel) / The economic situation is improving.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ After a possessive (his, their) or an article (a, the) → usually a noun.</p>\n<p>▸ Before a noun → adjective; after be / seem / become → adjective.</p>\n<p>▸ Linking verbs (look, feel, seem, sound) take adjectives: She looks happy (not happily).</p>\n<p>▸ Check spelling changes: beauty → beautiful, happy → happiness, decide → decision, explain → explanation.</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">أسئلة صيغ الكلمات من أكثر أسئلة STEP شيوعًا، والحل أن تنظر إلى موقع الفراغ: بعد أداة التعريف أو الصفة أو صفة الملكية نحتاج اسمًا، وبعد فعل be أو قبل الاسم نحتاج صفة، ولوصف الفعل نحتاج ظرفًا.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تساعد اللواحق على معرفة نوع الكلمة: tion وment وness وity للأسماء، وful وless وive وous وable للصفات، وize وen وify للأفعال، وly للظروف.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">والسوابق مثل un وdis وin وim وil وir تعطي معنى النفي، وهناك كلمات متشابهة يجب التمييز بينها مثل affect (فعل) وeffect (اسم)، وeconomic (اقتصادي) وeconomical (موفّر).</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>He spoke very good.</em> <strong>→ ✓ He spoke very well.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لوصف الفعل نستخدم الظرف well.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>She was very interesting in the story.</em> <strong>→ ✓ She was very interested in the story.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شعور الشخص بـ ed.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>The pollution effects our health.</em> <strong>→ ✓ The pollution affects our health.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">affect فعل وeffect اسم.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>It's unpossible.</em> <strong>→ ✓ It's impossible.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">قبل p نستخدم im.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>They need more informations and advices.</em> <strong>→ ✓ They need more information and advice.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">أسماء غير معدودة لا تُجمع.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>She looks happily.</em> <strong>→ ✓ She looks happy.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد look بمعنى يبدو نستخدم صفة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Noun: The beauty of AlUla is amazing.</p>\n<p>Adjective: AlUla is beautiful.</p>\n<p>Adverb: The rocks are beautifully shaped.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Identify the slot: what comes before and after the blank?</p>\n<p>2. Article / adjective / possessive + ___ → noun; be / seem + ___ → adjective; verb + ___ (manner) → adverb.</p>\n<p>3. Use suffixes to identify the options quickly.</p>\n<p>4. -ed for feelings, -ing for causes.</p>\n<p>5. Watch for confusing pairs: affect / effect, economic / economical, historic / historical.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حدّد موقع الفراغ وما قبله وما بعده، ثم استخدم اللواحق لتعرف نوع كل خيار، وتذكّر الفرق بين صفات ed وing والكلمات المتشابهة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. The ______ of the new hospital took three years.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. construct B. constructive C. construction D. constructively</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The blank comes after The and before of → a noun.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> construct (v) → construction (n).</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد The وقبل of نحتاج اسمًا: construction.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Students should use their time ______.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. wise B. wisely C. wisdom D. wiser</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The blank describes how they use their time (a verb).</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> To describe a verb → adverb.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> wisely. The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لوصف الفعل نستخدم الظرف wisely.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. The (A) <u>new</u> law will (B) <u>have</u> a big (C) <u>affect</u> on (D) <u>small</u> businesses.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. new B. have C. affect D. small</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> After a big we need a noun.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> affect is a verb; the noun is effect.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: The new law will have a big effect on small businesses. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد a big نحتاج اسمًا: effect.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 C · 2 B · 3 D · Worked examples: Example 1 C · Example 2 B · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"We were all ______ by the news of his recovery.","o":["relieved","relieving","relief","relieve"],"k":0,"e":"How people felt → -ed adjective.","h":"شعور الأشخاص بـ ed."},{"n":2,"s":"The ______ of the project depends on teamwork.","o":["success","succeed","successful","successfully"],"k":0,"e":"After The → noun.","h":"بعد The اسم."},{"n":3,"s":"This road is very ______ at night. Drive carefully.","o":["danger","dangerously","dangerous","endanger"],"k":2,"e":"After very and be → adjective.","h":"بعد be صفة."},{"n":4,"s":"She speaks English ______.","o":["fluently","fluent","fluency","fluentness"],"k":0,"e":"Describes speaks → adverb.","h":"لوصف الفعل ظرف."},{"n":5,"s":"It is ______ to park in front of a hospital entrance.","o":["unlegal","illegal","inlegal","dislegal"],"k":1,"e":"legal → illegal (il- before l).","h":"il قبل l."},{"n":6,"s":"The teacher gave us a clear ______ of the rule.","o":["explanation","explain","explanatory","explaination"],"k":0,"e":"After a clear → noun; spelling explanation.","h":"اسم بتهجئة صحيحة."},{"n":7,"s":"Smoking can ______ your health badly.","o":["effect","effective","affect","affection"],"k":2,"e":"After can → verb affect.","h":"بعد can فعل affect."},{"n":8,"s":"We need to ______ the road because there is too much traffic.","o":["wide","width","widely","widen"],"k":3,"e":"After to → verb: wide → widen.","h":"بعد to فعل widen."},{"n":9,"s":"I'm sorry. I ______ your question.","o":["disunderstood","ununderstood","overunderstood","misunderstood"],"k":3,"e":"mis- = wrongly.","h":"mis تعني خطأً."},{"n":10,"s":"The lecture was so ______ that half the students fell asleep.","o":["bored","boring","bore","boredom"],"k":1,"e":"What causes the feeling → -ing adjective.","h":"سبب الشعور ing."},{"n":11,"s":"The company is looking for ______ workers who can solve problems.","o":["create","creation","creative","creatively"],"k":2,"e":"Before a noun (workers) → adjective.","h":"قبل الاسم صفة."},{"n":12,"s":"Saving water is the ______ of every citizen.","o":["responsible","responsibility","responsibly","respond"],"k":1,"e":"After the → noun.","h":"بعد the اسم."},{"n":13,"s":"This small car is very ______; it uses little fuel.","o":["economical","economic","economy","economically"],"k":0,"e":"Saving money / fuel → economical.","h":"موفّر economical."},{"n":14,"s":"Her ______ to help others makes her popular.","o":["willing","willingly","will","willingness"],"k":3,"e":"After Her → noun.","h":"بعد Her اسم."},{"n":15,"s":"The instructions were ______ written, so nobody understood them.","o":["bad","badly","badness","worse"],"k":1,"e":"Describes written (a verb form) → adverb.","h":"لوصف الفعل ظرف."},{"n":16,"s":"It is ______ for a person to live without water for many days.","o":["unpossible","inpossible","impossible","dispossible"],"k":2,"e":"possible → impossible (im- before p).","h":"im قبل p."},{"n":17,"s":"The soup tastes ______. Can I have some more?","o":["deliciously","deliciousness","delicacy","delicious"],"k":3,"e":"After tastes (linking verb) → adjective.","h":"بعد tastes صفة."},{"n":18,"s":"Scientists are studying the ______ of climate change on coral reefs.","o":["affects","effective","affected","effects"],"k":3,"e":"After the → noun effects.","h":"بعد the اسم effects."},{"n":19,"s":"Al-Masmak is an important ______ building in Riyadh.","o":["history","historian","historic","historically"],"k":2,"e":"Before building → adjective; historic = famous in history.","h":"صفة historic."},{"n":20,"s":"Many young people feel ______ about their future careers.","o":["anxious","anxiety","anxiously","anxiousness"],"k":0,"e":"After feel (linking verb) → adjective.","h":"بعد feel صفة."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"(A) The (B) develop of the new (C) metro (D) system took years.","o":["The","develop","metro","system"],"k":1,"e":"After The → noun development.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"She (A) answered all the (B) questions (C) correct and (D) quickly.","o":["answered","questions","correct","quickly"],"k":2,"e":"Describes answered → adverb correctly.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"The (A) students were (B) exciting about the (C) trip to (D) AlUla.","o":["students","exciting","trip","AlUla"],"k":1,"e":"How people feel → excited.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"Pollution has a (A) serious (B) effect on our (C) health and on the (D) economical growth of cities.","o":["serious","effect","health","economical"],"k":3,"e":"About the economy → economic.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"Her (A) kind and (B) generous (C) helped many (D) families.","o":["kind","generous","helped","families"],"k":2,"e":"After Her → nouns (kindness, generosity).","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"It is (A) unlegal to (B) drive without (C) a valid (D) licence.","o":["unlegal","drive","a","licence"],"k":0,"e":"legal → illegal.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"The (A) food at the (B) wedding (C) smelled (D) wonderfully.","o":["food","wedding","smelled","wonderfully"],"k":3,"e":"After smell (linking verb) → adjective.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"The (A) government plans to (B) modern the (C) old (D) airport.","o":["government","modern","old","airport"],"k":1,"e":"After to → verb modernize.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"We (A) need a (B) reliable and (C) efficiency (D) system.","o":["need","reliable","efficiency","system"],"k":2,"e":"Before a noun → adjective efficient.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"(A) Success people (B) usually (C) work (D) hard.","o":["Success","usually","work","hard"],"k":0,"e":"Before people → adjective successful.","h":""}]}],"n":30},{"id":"5.5","t":"Parallel Structure, Word Order and Embedded Questions","html":"<p><strong>Unit 5 · Lesson 5.5 · CEFR B2+ · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Keep items in a series grammatically parallel (nouns with nouns, -ing with -ing, to + verb with to + verb).</p>\n<p>2. Place adverbs and multiple adjectives in the correct order.</p>\n<p>3. Use statement word order in embedded questions (Do you know where the library is?).</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يحافظ الطالب على التوازي النحوي بين عناصر السلسلة: اسم مع اسم وing مع ing وto مع to.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يرتّب الظروف والصفات المتعددة ترتيبًا صحيحًا.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يستخدم ترتيب الجملة الخبرية في الأسئلة المضمّنة.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. She likes swimming, reading and ______.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. to cook B. cooking C. cooks D. cook</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Can you tell me where ______?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. is the station B. the station is</p>\n<p>C. does the station D. station is the</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. He bought ______.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. a leather black old bag B. an old black leather bag</p>\n<p>C. a black old leather bag D. an leather old black bag</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Parallel structure</strong></p>\n<p><strong>X, Y and Z must be the same grammatical form</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The job requires patience, skill and experience. (nouns) / I enjoy hiking, swimming and cycling. (-ing)</em></p>\n<p><strong>Correlative pairs</strong></p>\n<p><strong>both … and · either … or · neither … nor · not only … but also + the SAME form</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. She is not only clever but also hard-working.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Comparisons</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Compare like with like</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The weather in Abha is cooler than the weather (that) in Riyadh. / … than that in Riyadh.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Adjective order</strong></p>\n<p><strong>opinion → size → age → shape → colour → origin → material → purpose + noun</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. a lovely small old round brown Saudi wooden coffee table</em></p>\n<p><strong>Adverb position</strong></p>\n<p><strong>frequency before the main verb / after be · manner, place, time usually at the end (manner → place → time)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. She always studies hard at the library in the evening.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Embedded (indirect) questions</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Do you know / Can you tell me / I wonder / I'm not sure + wh-word / if + subject + verb</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Do you know what time it is? I wonder if he has arrived.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Noun clauses as subject</strong></p>\n<p><strong>What / Whether / How + subject + verb + main verb</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. What he said was true. How they did it is a mystery.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Parallel structure in lists and pairs.</strong></p>\n<p>All items joined by and, or, but, both … and, either … or must have the same form.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Students should read carefully, think clearly and answer quickly.</p>\n<p>▸ The new park is safe, clean and beautiful.</p>\n<p>▸ He wants either to study medicine or to become a pilot.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Parallel comparisons.</strong></p>\n<p>Compare the same kind of thing.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ The population of Riyadh is larger than that of Jeddah.</p>\n<p>▸ Writing an essay is harder than answering multiple-choice questions.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Order of adjectives and adverbs.</strong></p>\n<p>English has a natural order for several adjectives and for adverbs at the end of a sentence.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ My grandfather has a beautiful old wooden chest.</p>\n<p>▸ We usually meet at the café on Thursdays.</p>\n<p>▸ She sang beautifully at the ceremony last night.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. Embedded questions.</strong></p>\n<p>Questions inside other sentences use statement word order — no do / does / did and no inversion.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Could you tell me where the nearest pharmacy is?</p>\n<p>▸ I don't know why she left early.</p>\n<p>▸ Do you remember if we locked the door?</p>\n<p>▸ What the teacher said surprised everyone.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ ✗ I like reading, to swim and cook. ✓ I like reading, swimming and cooking.</p>\n<p>▸ ✗ Can you tell me where is the bank? ✓ Can you tell me where the bank is?</p>\n<p>▸ Use if / whether for yes / no embedded questions: I'm not sure whether he is coming.</p>\n<p>▸ Do not put an adverb between a verb and its object: ✗ She speaks very well English. ✓ She speaks English very well.</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">التوازي يعني أن تكون العناصر المعطوفة بـ and وor وboth … and وeither … or من النوع النحوي نفسه، فنقول reading, swimming and cooking لا reading, to swim and cook.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">للصفات المتعددة قبل الاسم ترتيب ثابت: الرأي ثم الحجم ثم العمر ثم الشكل ثم اللون ثم الأصل ثم المادة ثم الغرض، والظروف في آخر الجملة تأتي غالبًا بترتيب: الطريقة ثم المكان ثم الزمان.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">السؤال المضمّن داخل جملة أخرى يأتي بترتيب الجملة الخبرية دون do أو does أو did ودون تقديم الفعل، مثل Do you know where the library is?</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I like reading, to swim and cook.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I like reading, swimming and cooking.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">العناصر المعطوفة بالصيغة نفسها.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Can you tell me where is the station?</em> <strong>→ ✓ Can you tell me where the station is?</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">السؤال المضمّن بترتيب الخبر.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I don't know what time does the shop open.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I don't know what time the shop opens.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا does في السؤال المضمّن.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>a black big car</em> <strong>→ ✓ a big black car</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الحجم قبل اللون.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>He speaks very well English.</em> <strong>→ ✓ He speaks English very well.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا نفصل بين الفعل ومفعوله.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>The weather in Abha is cooler than Riyadh.</em> <strong>→ ✓ The weather in Abha is cooler than that in Riyadh.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">نقارن الطقس بالطقس.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Not parallel: She is smart, funny and has kindness.</p>\n<p>Parallel: She is smart, funny and kind.</p>\n<p>Direct question: Where is the bank? → Embedded: Do you know where the bank is?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. In a list, find the form of the first item and make the others match.</p>\n<p>2. With both / either / neither / not only, check the words right after each part.</p>\n<p>3. Embedded question: wh-word / if + subject + verb; reject options with is / does before the subject.</p>\n<p>4. Adjectives: opinion before size before age before colour before material.</p>\n<p>5. In comparisons, check that the two things compared are the same type (that of / those of).</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">في السلسلة اجعل جميع العناصر بصيغة العنصر الأول، وفي السؤال المضمّن استخدم ترتيب الخبر، ورتّب الصفات حسب القاعدة، وقارن الأشياء المتماثلة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. The new manager is friendly, efficient and ______.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. has experience B. experience</p>\n<p>C. experienced D. with experience</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The list has two adjectives: friendly, efficient.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> The third item must be an adjective too.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> experienced. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">العنصران الأولان صفتان فيكون الثالث صفة.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. I wonder ______ the museum is open on Fridays.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. if B. is C. does D. that if</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> This is an embedded yes / no question.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Embedded yes / no questions use if / whether + statement order.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is A.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">السؤال المضمّن بنعم أو لا يبدأ بـ if.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Could you (A) <u>tell</u> me (B) <u>what time</u> (C) <u>does</u> the (D) <u>train</u> leave?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. tell B. what time C. does D. train</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> This is an embedded question inside Could you tell me …</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Embedded questions do not use does.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: Could you tell me what time the train leaves? The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا does في السؤال المضمّن.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 B · 2 B · 3 B · Worked examples: Example 1 C · Example 2 A · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"My hobbies are reading, drawing and ______.","o":["to swim","swimming","swim","I swim"],"k":1,"e":"Parallel -ing forms.","h":"التوازي بـ ing."},{"n":2,"s":"Do you know where ______?","o":["is the post office","does the post office","the post office does","the post office is"],"k":3,"e":"Embedded question → statement order.","h":"ترتيب الخبر."},{"n":3,"s":"She bought a ______ for her father.","o":["beautiful brown leather wallet","brown beautiful leather wallet","leather brown beautiful wallet","beautiful leather brown wallet"],"k":0,"e":"opinion → colour → material.","h":"الرأي ثم اللون ثم المادة."},{"n":4,"s":"The job needs someone who is patient, careful and ______.","o":["relies","reliability","to rely","reliable"],"k":3,"e":"Parallel adjectives.","h":"صفات متوازية."},{"n":5,"s":"I'm not sure ______ he will come to the party.","o":["that whether","whether","does","will"],"k":1,"e":"Embedded yes / no → whether.","h":"whether للسؤال المضمّن."},{"n":6,"s":"He speaks ______.","o":["Arabic and English fluently","fluently Arabic and English","Arabic fluently and English","and English Arabic fluently"],"k":0,"e":"Verb + object + adverb.","h":"الفعل ثم المفعول ثم الظرف."},{"n":7,"s":"The teacher asked us to read the text, ______ the questions and check our answers.","o":["answer","answering","to answering","answered"],"k":0,"e":"Parallel base verbs after to: read, answer, check.","h":"التوازي بين الأفعال."},{"n":8,"s":"Can you tell me how much ______?","o":["does this jacket cost","costs this jacket","this jacket costs","is this jacket cost"],"k":2,"e":"Embedded question → statement order.","h":"ترتيب الخبر."},{"n":9,"s":"Both my brother ______ my sister study at King Saud University.","o":["and","or","nor","but"],"k":0,"e":"both … and.","h":"both … and."},{"n":10,"s":"We usually have lunch ______.","o":["on Fridays at home","at home usually on Fridays","at home on Fridays","Fridays on at home"],"k":2,"e":"Place before time.","h":"المكان قبل الزمان."},{"n":11,"s":"Living in a big city is more expensive than ______ in a village.","o":["to live","live","lives","living"],"k":3,"e":"Compare -ing with -ing.","h":"مقارنة ing مع ing."},{"n":12,"s":"I wonder why ______ so late.","o":["is the bus","does the bus","the bus is","the bus does"],"k":2,"e":"Embedded wh-question → statement order.","h":"ترتيب الخبر."},{"n":13,"s":"They have a ______ in their garden.","o":["old large palm tree","palm large old tree","large palm old tree","large old palm tree"],"k":3,"e":"size → age → type noun.","h":"الحجم ثم العمر."},{"n":14,"s":"The film was not only long ______ boring.","o":["but also","and also","but too","also"],"k":0,"e":"not only … but also.","h":"not only … but also."},{"n":15,"s":"______ he said at the meeting surprised everyone.","o":["That what","Which","What","It"],"k":2,"e":"Noun clause as subject → What.","h":"What كفاعل."},{"n":16,"s":"The climate of Abha is cooler than ______ of Riyadh.","o":["that","those","it","this"],"k":0,"e":"Compare climate with climate → that of.","h":"that of للمقارنة."},{"n":17,"s":"She is good at writing reports, giving presentations and ______ meetings.","o":["to organize","organizing","organize","organization"],"k":1,"e":"Parallel -ing after at.","h":"التوازي بـ ing."},{"n":18,"s":"Nobody knows how ______ the problem.","o":["did they solve","solved they","they solved","do they solve"],"k":2,"e":"Embedded question → statement order.","h":"ترتيب الخبر."},{"n":19,"s":"You can either pay by card ______ in cash.","o":["and","or","nor","but"],"k":1,"e":"either … or.","h":"either … or."},{"n":20,"s":"The prices in this shop are higher than ______ in the market.","o":["that","them","it","those"],"k":3,"e":"Compare prices (plural) → those.","h":"those للجمع."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"I enjoy (A) reading, (B) to swim and (C) playing (D) football.","o":["reading","to swim","playing","football"],"k":1,"e":"Parallel -ing forms.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"Can you (A) tell me (B) where (C) is the (D) bank?","o":["tell","where","is","bank"],"k":2,"e":"Embedded question → statement order.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"(A) She is (B) intelligent, (C) hard-working and (D) has kindness.","o":["She","intelligent","hard-working","has kindness"],"k":3,"e":"Parallel adjectives.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"My (A) uncle bought a (B) black big (C) new (D) car.","o":["uncle","black big","new","car"],"k":1,"e":"size → age → colour.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"(A) I don't know what time (B) does the (C) shop (D) open.","o":["I don't know","does","shop","open"],"k":1,"e":"No does in an embedded question.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"The (A) weather in Taif is (B) cooler (C) than (D) Riyadh.","o":["weather","cooler","than","Riyadh"],"k":3,"e":"Compare weather with weather → that in Riyadh.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"He (A) speaks (B) very well (C) English and (D) French.","o":["speaks","very well","English","French"],"k":1,"e":"Do not put the adverb between the verb and its object.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"The (A) course teaches students how to (B) think (C) critically and (D) writing clearly.","o":["course","think","critically","writing"],"k":3,"e":"Parallel base verbs: think, write.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"(A) Not only (B) she (C) is a doctor, but she is also (D) a writer.","o":["Not only","she","is","a"],"k":0,"e":"Not only at the start → inversion.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"Do you (A) remember (B) if (C) did we lock (D) the door?","o":["remember","if","did we","the"],"k":2,"e":"Embedded question → statement order (we locked).","h":""}]}],"n":30},{"id":"5.6","t":"Dependent Prepositions and Collocations (linked to Appendix B)","html":"<p><strong>Unit 5 · Lesson 5.6 · CEFR B2+ · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Use verb / adjective / noun + preposition combinations (depend on, responsible for, reason for).</p>\n<p>2. Avoid the extra or missing prepositions typical of Arabic speakers (discuss about, enter to, listen music).</p>\n<p>3. Choose strong collocations (make a decision, do research, pay attention, take part in).</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يستخدم الطالب حروف الجر الملازمة للأفعال والصفات والأسماء مثل depend on وresponsible for وreason for.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يتجنب الزيادة أو الحذف في حروف الجر الشائعين لدى المتعلمين العرب مثل discuss about وenter to وlisten music.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يختار المتلازمات اللفظية القوية مثل make a decision وdo research وpay attention.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Our success depends ______ teamwork.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. of B. on C. from D. at</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. We need to ______ a decision quickly.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. do B. take place C. make D. have done</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. She is interested ______ space science.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. in B. on C. about D. for</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Verb + preposition</strong></p>\n<p><strong>depend on · consist of · apologize for · insist on · succeed in · belong to · rely on · suffer from · approve of · participate in</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The team consists of eleven players.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Adjective + preposition</strong></p>\n<p><strong>interested in · good at · afraid of · proud of · responsible for · famous for · similar to · different from · aware of · keen on</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Jeddah is famous for its old houses.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Noun + preposition</strong></p>\n<p><strong>reason for · solution to · increase in · effect on · demand for · advantage of · lack of · access to</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. There is a lack of water in the region.</em></p>\n<p><strong>No preposition (Arab Learner traps)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>discuss · enter · reach · marry · answer · contact · attend · approach + direct object</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. We discussed the plan. He entered the room.</em></p>\n<p><strong>make collocations</strong></p>\n<p><strong>make a decision / a mistake / progress / an effort / a plan / money / a difference</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Small actions can make a difference.</em></p>\n<p><strong>do collocations</strong></p>\n<p><strong>do research / homework / business / your best / damage / exercise</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Scientists are doing research on desert plants.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Other strong collocations</strong></p>\n<p><strong>pay attention · take part in · take place · have an impact on · raise awareness · meet a deadline · heavy traffic · strong coffee</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The festival takes place every February.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Prepositions are fixed — learn the whole chunk.</strong></p>\n<p>Many verbs, adjectives and nouns are followed by one particular preposition.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Whether we go depends on the weather.</p>\n<p>▸ My grandfather is proud of his farm.</p>\n<p>▸ Is there a solution to this problem?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. After a preposition, use a noun or -ing.</strong></p>\n<p>If a verb follows a dependent preposition, it takes the -ing form.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ He is good at solving puzzles.</p>\n<p>▸ She apologized for being late.</p>\n<p>▸ They succeeded in finishing the project early.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Verbs that take NO preposition.</strong></p>\n<p>Arabic often uses a preposition where English does not.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ We discussed the problem. (not discussed about)</p>\n<p>▸ The plane reached Riyadh at noon. (not reached to)</p>\n<p>▸ He married a teacher. (not married with)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. Collocations make English sound natural.</strong></p>\n<p>Some words simply go together; using the wrong partner sounds unnatural and is often tested.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Please pay attention to the instructions.</p>\n<p>▸ Many students took part in the competition.</p>\n<p>▸ The new law will have a positive impact on the environment.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ Some words change meaning with the preposition: agree with (a person) / agree to (a plan) / agree on (a decision).</p>\n<p>▸ different from (preferred in exams) — not different than / different of.</p>\n<p>▸ married to, not married with; listen to music, not listen music.</p>\n<p>▸ See Appendix B for 120 prepositional verbs with examples.</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حروف الجر الملازمة لا تخضع لقاعدة ثابتة، بل تُحفظ مع الكلمة مثل depend on وinterested in وreason for، وإذا جاء بعدها فعل فإنه يأتي بصيغة ing.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">يقع المتعلم العربي في خطأ إضافة حرف جر لا تحتاجه الإنجليزية، مثل discuss about وenter to وreach to وmarry with، أو حذف حرف جر تحتاجه مثل listen music وwait me.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المتلازمات اللفظية كلمات تأتي معًا عادةً، مثل make a decision وdo research وpay attention وtake part in، واستخدام البديل الخاطئ مثل do a decision يُعدّ خطأ في أسئلة STEP.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>We discussed about the plan.</em> <strong>→ ✓ We discussed the plan.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">discuss لا تحتاج about.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>He entered to the room.</em> <strong>→ ✓ He entered the room.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">enter لا تحتاج to.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I like listening music.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I like listening to music.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">listen تحتاج to.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>She is married with an engineer.</em> <strong>→ ✓ She is married to an engineer.</strong></p>\n<p><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">married to.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>It depends of the weather.</em> <strong>→ ✓ It depends on the weather.</strong></p>\n<p><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">depend on.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>We did a decision.</em> <strong>→ ✓ We made a decision.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المتلازمة make a decision.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>agree with someone · agree to a request · agree on a plan</p>\n<p>interested in (adjective) · interest in (noun) · interesting (adjective for things)</p>\n<p>make a mistake · do homework · take part · pay attention</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Look at the word BEFORE the blank and recall its fixed preposition.</p>\n<p>2. If a verb follows the preposition, choose -ing.</p>\n<p>3. Remember verbs that take a direct object (discuss, enter, reach, marry, attend).</p>\n<p>4. For collocations, choose the verb that naturally goes with the noun (make / do / take / pay).</p>\n<p>5. STEP error items often add about / to / with where none is needed.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">انظر إلى الكلمة قبل الفراغ وتذكّر حرف الجر الملازم لها، واستخدم ing بعد حرف الجر، وتذكّر الأفعال التي لا تحتاج حرف جر، واختر الفعل المناسب في المتلازمات.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. The new park consists ______ three gardens and a small lake.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. in B. from C. of D. with</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The verb is consist.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> consist + of.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">consist of.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Many volunteers ______ part in the beach clean-up last Friday.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. made B. took C. did D. had</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The collocation is take part in.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Past tense → took.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المتلازمة take part in.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. The (A) <u>students</u> (B) <u>discussed</u> (C) <u>about</u> the (D) <u>project</u> for an hour.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. students B. discussed C. about D. project</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> discuss takes a direct object.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> about must be removed.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: The students discussed the project for an hour. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">discuss لا تحتاج about.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 B · 2 C · 3 A · Worked examples: Example 1 C · Example 2 B · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Our plans for the weekend depend ______ the weather.","o":["of","from","at","on"],"k":3,"e":"depend on.","h":"depend on."},{"n":2,"s":"My little sister is afraid ______ the dark.","o":["from","on","of","with"],"k":2,"e":"afraid of.","h":"afraid of."},{"n":3,"s":"Taif is famous ______ its roses.","o":["for","of","with","by"],"k":0,"e":"famous for.","h":"famous for."},{"n":4,"s":"Please pay ______ to the safety instructions.","o":["care","attention","notice","interest"],"k":1,"e":"Collocation: pay attention.","h":"pay attention."},{"n":5,"s":"He apologized ______ breaking the window.","o":["for","of","about","on"],"k":0,"e":"apologize for + -ing.","h":"apologize for."},{"n":6,"s":"Everyone makes ______ when learning a new language.","o":["errors doing","faults","mistakes","wrongs"],"k":2,"e":"Collocation: make mistakes.","h":"make mistakes."},{"n":7,"s":"This bag belongs ______ my brother.","o":["for","with","to","of"],"k":2,"e":"belong to.","h":"belong to."},{"n":8,"s":"The team succeeded ______ winning the cup.","o":["in","on","at","to"],"k":0,"e":"succeed in + -ing.","h":"succeed in."},{"n":9,"s":"She is very good ______ maths.","o":["in","on","at","for"],"k":2,"e":"good at.","h":"good at."},{"n":10,"s":"Scientists are ______ research on new energy sources.","o":["making","doing","taking","having"],"k":1,"e":"Collocation: do research.","h":"do research."},{"n":11,"s":"The plane ______ Riyadh two hours late.","o":["reached to","arrived","got","reached"],"k":3,"e":"reach + direct object (no to).","h":"reach دون to."},{"n":12,"s":"Our school is different ______ other schools in the city.","o":["from","of","than of","with"],"k":0,"e":"different from.","h":"different from."},{"n":13,"s":"There has been a big increase ______ the number of tourists.","o":["of","in","on","at"],"k":1,"e":"increase in.","h":"increase in."},{"n":14,"s":"Who is responsible ______ cleaning the classroom today?","o":["of","for","on","about"],"k":1,"e":"responsible for.","h":"responsible for."},{"n":15,"s":"We have to ______ a decision before Thursday.","o":["do","take place","have done","make"],"k":3,"e":"Collocation: make a decision.","h":"make a decision."},{"n":16,"s":"Many students suffer ______ stress before exams.","o":["from","of","with","by"],"k":0,"e":"suffer from.","h":"suffer from."},{"n":17,"s":"Pollution has a negative effect ______ health.","o":["in","on","to","for"],"k":1,"e":"effect on.","h":"effect on."},{"n":18,"s":"Hessa insisted ______ paying for everyone.","o":["to","for","in","on"],"k":3,"e":"insist on + -ing.","h":"insist on."},{"n":19,"s":"The meeting will take ______ in the main hall.","o":["part","time","place","turn"],"k":2,"e":"Collocation: take place = happen.","h":"take place."},{"n":20,"s":"Students need easy access ______ the library.","o":["for","at","in","to"],"k":3,"e":"access to.","h":"access to."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"We (A) discussed (B) about the (C) new (D) timetable.","o":["discussed","about","new","timetable"],"k":1,"e":"discuss takes no preposition.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"(A) Interested on photography, she (B) joined (C) the (D) club.","o":["Interested on","joined","the","club"],"k":0,"e":"interested in.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"My success (A) in the exam (B) depended (C) largely (D) of my hard work.","o":["in","depended","largely","of"],"k":3,"e":"depend on.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"The (A) teacher (B) entered (C) to (D) the classroom quietly.","o":["teacher","entered","to","the"],"k":2,"e":"enter takes no preposition.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"Many (A) students made (B) careless (C) errors because they didn't (D) make attention.","o":["students","careless","errors","make"],"k":3,"e":"Collocation: pay attention.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"He (A) is married with a doctor (B) who (C) works (D) in Jeddah.","o":["is married with","who","works","in"],"k":0,"e":"married to.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"I (A) like (B) listening (C) music (D) in the car.","o":["like","listening","music","in"],"k":2,"e":"listen to.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"(A) The reason (B) of the (C) delay was (D) the storm.","o":["The","of","delay","the"],"k":1,"e":"reason for.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"Thousands of (A) runners (B) from (C) many countries (D) made part in the marathon.","o":["runners","from","many","made part"],"k":3,"e":"Collocation: take part in.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"(A) We are proud with our (B) team, (C) which won the (D) cup.","o":["We are proud with","team","which","cup"],"k":0,"e":"proud of.","h":""}]}],"n":30},{"id":"5.7","t":"Advanced Comparison and Linking (the more … the more, whereas, nevertheless, provided that)","html":"<p><strong>Unit 5 · Lesson 5.7 · CEFR B2+ · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Use the + comparative … the + comparative.</p>\n<p>2. Use whereas, while, nevertheless, however, moreover, therefore and provided that with correct meaning and punctuation.</p>\n<p>3. Use comparative modifiers (far, much, considerably, slightly, by far, twice as … as).</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يستخدم الطالب تركيب the + صيغة المقارنة … the + صيغة المقارنة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يستخدم أدوات الربط whereas وwhile وnevertheless وhowever وmoreover وtherefore وprovided that بالمعنى وعلامات الترقيم الصحيحة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يستخدم معدِّلات المقارنة مثل far وmuch وconsiderably وslightly وby far وtwice as … as.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. The more you practise, the ______ you become.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. good B. best C. better D. more good</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Riyadh is hot and dry, ______ Jeddah is hot and humid.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. whereas B. therefore C. moreover D. despite</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. This phone is ______ more expensive than that one.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. very B. much C. too D. so</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>The … the …</strong></p>\n<p><strong>The + comparative (+ subject + verb), the + comparative (+ subject + verb)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The harder you study, the higher your score will be. The sooner, the better.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Comparative modifiers</strong></p>\n<p><strong>much / far / a lot / considerably / slightly / a little + comparative</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The new road is far safer than the old one.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Superlative modifiers</strong></p>\n<p><strong>by far / easily + the + superlative · the second / third + superlative</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. This is by far the best restaurant in town. Jeddah is the second largest city.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Multiples</strong></p>\n<p><strong>twice / three times + as + adjective + as · half as … as</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The new stadium is twice as big as the old one.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Contrast linkers</strong></p>\n<p><strong>whereas / while + clause (within one sentence) · However, / Nevertheless, / On the other hand, (new sentence)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Ali likes tea, whereas his brother prefers coffee. The task was hard. Nevertheless, we finished it.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Addition and result linkers</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Moreover, / Furthermore, / In addition, (addition) · Therefore, / As a result, / Consequently, (result)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The hotel is cheap. Moreover, it is near the beach.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Condition linkers</strong></p>\n<p><strong>provided (that) / providing / as long as / on condition that + present simple</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. You may leave early provided that you finish your work.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. The … the … shows two things changing together.</strong></p>\n<p>When one thing increases or decreases, the other changes too.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ The more you read, the more you learn.</p>\n<p>▸ The older my grandfather gets, the wiser he becomes.</p>\n<p>▸ The faster you drive, the more dangerous it is.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Making comparisons stronger or weaker.</strong></p>\n<p>Use much / far / considerably for big differences and slightly / a little for small ones; never very with comparatives.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Life in the city is much busier than life in the village.</p>\n<p>▸ The second test was slightly easier than the first.</p>\n<p>▸ Saudi Arabia is by far the largest country in the Arabian Peninsula.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Contrast inside a sentence vs between sentences.</strong></p>\n<p>whereas / while join two clauses; however / nevertheless start a new sentence or clause after a semicolon.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Some students prefer online classes, whereas others prefer face-to-face lessons.</p>\n<p>▸ The weather was terrible. However, the match continued.</p>\n<p>▸ He was very tired; nevertheless, he finished his shift.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. Adding ideas, showing results and conditions formally.</strong></p>\n<p>These linkers are common in academic writing and STEP Composition Analysis items.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ The project is expensive. Furthermore, it will take years.</p>\n<p>▸ Fuel prices rose. As a result, many people started using the metro.</p>\n<p>▸ Visitors may enter the mosque provided that they dress modestly.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ ✗ very better ✓ much better · ✗ more better ✓ better.</p>\n<p>▸ The … the … needs two comparatives and two clauses (or a fixed phrase: the sooner the better).</p>\n<p>▸ however and nevertheless are adverbs, not conjunctions: use a full stop or semicolon before them, and a comma after.</p>\n<p>▸ whereas / while for contrast cannot start a second sentence on their own after a full stop in formal writing.</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تركيب the + صيغة المقارنة … the + صيغة المقارنة يعبّر عن أمرين يتغيران معًا، مثل The more you read, the more you learn أي «كلما قرأت أكثر تعلمت أكثر».</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لتقوية المقارنة نستخدم much أو far أو considerably، ولتخفيفها slightly أو a little، ولا نستخدم very مع صيغة المقارنة. ومع التفضيل نستخدم by far، وللمضاعفة twice as … as.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">whereas وwhile تربطان جملتين متعارضتين داخل جملة واحدة، أما however وnevertheless فتبدأان جملة جديدة أو تأتيان بعد فاصلة منقوطة، وmoreover وfurthermore للإضافة، وtherefore وas a result للنتيجة، وprovided that للشرط.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>The more you study, the best your score.</em> <strong>→ ✓ The more you study, the better your score.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">نحتاج صيغة المقارنة في الجزأين.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>This car is very faster than mine.</em> <strong>→ ✓ This car is much faster than mine.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا very مع المقارنة.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>The new stadium is twice bigger than the old one.</em> <strong>→ ✓ The new stadium is twice as big as the old one.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المضاعفة بـ twice as … as.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I was tired, however I continued.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I was tired; however, I continued.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">however تحتاج فاصلة منقوطة أو نقطة قبلها.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Ali is tall. Whereas his brother is short.</em> <strong>→ ✓ Ali is tall, whereas his brother is short.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">whereas تربط داخل الجملة.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>You can go provided that you will finish your work.</em> <strong>→ ✓ You can go provided that you finish your work.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد provided that المضارع البسيط.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>whereas: Huda likes art, whereas Reem likes science. (one sentence)</p>\n<p>however: Huda likes art. However, Reem likes science. (two sentences)</p>\n<p>nevertheless: It rained heavily. Nevertheless, the race went ahead. (surprising result)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. The … the …: check for two comparatives (the more … the better).</p>\n<p>2. Before a comparative, choose much / far / slightly — not very.</p>\n<p>3. Within one sentence → whereas / while; at the start of a new sentence → However / Nevertheless.</p>\n<p>4. Match the linker to the meaning: contrast, addition, result or condition.</p>\n<p>5. Multiples need as … as: twice as long as.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">في تركيب the … the تأكد من وجود صيغتي مقارنة، ولا تستخدم very مع المقارنة، واختر whereas داخل الجملة وHowever في بداية جملة جديدة، وطابق أداة الربط مع المعنى.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. The earlier you leave, ______ traffic you will meet.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. the less B. less C. the least D. the fewer than</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The sentence starts with The earlier … → The … the … structure.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> The second part also needs the + comparative.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> the less. The answer is A.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تركيب the … the يحتاج the + المقارنة في الجزأين.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. The test was difficult. ______, most students passed.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Whereas B. Nevertheless C. Because D. Moreover</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The second sentence is a surprising contrast.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> A new sentence + contrast → Nevertheless / However.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تعارض في جملة جديدة: Nevertheless.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. The (A) <u>new</u> metro is (B) <u>very</u> (C) <u>faster</u> than (D) <u>the</u> bus.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. new B. very C. faster D. the</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> very cannot modify a comparative.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Use much / far: much faster.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: The new metro is much faster than the bus. The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا very مع المقارنة؛ نستخدم much.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 C · 2 A · 3 B · Worked examples: Example 1 A · Example 2 B · Example 3 B","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"The more you exercise, the ______ you feel.","o":["healthy","healthier","healthiest","more healthy than"],"k":1,"e":"The … the … + comparative.","h":"تركيب the … the."},{"n":2,"s":"The new library is ______ bigger than the old one.","o":["much","very","too","so"],"k":0,"e":"much + comparative.","h":"much مع المقارنة."},{"n":3,"s":"Abha is cool in summer, ______ Riyadh is extremely hot.","o":["moreover","therefore","nevertheless","whereas"],"k":3,"e":"Contrast within a sentence → whereas.","h":"تعارض داخل الجملة whereas."},{"n":4,"s":"The bridge is twice ______ the old one.","o":["longer than","as long as","as longer as","long as"],"k":1,"e":"twice as + adjective + as.","h":"twice as … as."},{"n":5,"s":"It was raining heavily. ______, the match went ahead.","o":["Nevertheless","Whereas","Because","So that"],"k":0,"e":"Surprising contrast in a new sentence.","h":"تعارض في جملة جديدة."},{"n":6,"s":"This is ______ the best restaurant in the city.","o":["by far","very","much more","far more"],"k":0,"e":"by far + superlative.","h":"by far مع التفضيل."},{"n":7,"s":"The hotel is cheap. ______, it is close to the beach.","o":["However","Moreover","Whereas","Therefore"],"k":1,"e":"Adding a positive point → Moreover.","h":"إضافة Moreover."},{"n":8,"s":"You can borrow my laptop ______ you return it tomorrow.","o":["whereas","however","provided that","moreover"],"k":2,"e":"Condition → provided that.","h":"شرط provided that."},{"n":9,"s":"The roads were flooded. ______, the schools were closed.","o":["However","As a result","Whereas","In spite of"],"k":1,"e":"Result → As a result.","h":"نتيجة As a result."},{"n":10,"s":"The sooner we start, ______ we will finish.","o":["earlier","the earliest","more early","the earlier"],"k":3,"e":"The … the … with a comparative.","h":"the + المقارنة."},{"n":11,"s":"The second exam was ______ easier than the first one.","o":["very","too","slightly","so"],"k":2,"e":"slightly + comparative (small difference).","h":"slightly مع المقارنة."},{"n":12,"s":"Some people love the desert, ______ others prefer the sea.","o":["however","therefore","while","moreover"],"k":2,"e":"Contrast within a sentence → while.","h":"تعارض داخل الجملة while."},{"n":13,"s":"Jeddah is the ______ largest city in Saudi Arabia.","o":["second","two","secondly","more second"],"k":0,"e":"the second + superlative.","h":"the second + التفضيل."},{"n":14,"s":"The price of the new phone is three times ______ that of the old model.","o":["higher as","as high as","as higher than","more high"],"k":1,"e":"three times as + adjective + as.","h":"المضاعفة."},{"n":15,"s":"The plan was expensive; ______, the council approved it.","o":["whereas","nevertheless","because","so that"],"k":1,"e":"Semicolon + nevertheless (contrast).","h":"بعد الفاصلة المنقوطة nevertheless."},{"n":16,"s":"The more I learn about space, ______ interested I become.","o":["more","the most","the more","most"],"k":2,"e":"The … the more.","h":"the more."},{"n":17,"s":"He didn't study. ______, he failed the test.","o":["Therefore","However","Whereas","Moreover"],"k":0,"e":"Result → Therefore.","h":"نتيجة Therefore."},{"n":18,"s":"Life in the village is ______ less stressful than life in the city.","o":["very","more","too","far"],"k":3,"e":"far + comparative.","h":"far مع المقارنة."},{"n":19,"s":"The project will succeed ______ everyone works together.","o":["whereas","however","as long as","despite"],"k":2,"e":"Condition → as long as.","h":"شرط as long as."},{"n":20,"s":"The weather was perfect. ______, the beach was not crowded.","o":["However","Whereas","As long as","In addition"],"k":3,"e":"Adding another positive point → In addition.","h":"إضافة In addition."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"The (A) more you read, (B) the (C) best your (D) vocabulary becomes.","o":["more","the","best","vocabulary"],"k":2,"e":"The … the … needs a comparative: better.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"(A) This car is very faster than my (B) old one, (C) but it (D) uses more fuel.","o":["This car is very faster","old","but","uses"],"k":0,"e":"No very with comparatives.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"The new (A) hall is (B) twice (C) as (D) bigger as the old one.","o":["hall","twice","as","bigger"],"k":3,"e":"twice as + basic adjective + as.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"I (A) was very (B) tired, (C) however I (D) finished my work.","o":["was","tired","however","finished"],"k":2,"e":"however needs a semicolon or full stop before it.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"(A) Ali likes football. (B) Whereas his brother (C) prefers (D) tennis.","o":["Ali","Whereas","prefers","tennis"],"k":1,"e":"whereas joins two clauses in one sentence.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"You (A) can use the (B) car (C) provided that you (D) will drive carefully.","o":["can","car","provided that","will drive"],"k":3,"e":"After provided that → present simple.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"This is by far (A) the (B) better hotel (C) in (D) Abha.","o":["the","better","in","Abha"],"k":1,"e":"by far + superlative: the best.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"The (A) hotter it (B) gets, (C) more water (D) people drink.","o":["hotter","gets","more","people"],"k":2,"e":"The … the more: the second part needs the.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"The prices rose sharply. (A) Whereas, many (B) families (C) spent (D) less.","o":["Whereas","families","spent","less"],"k":0,"e":"Result in a new sentence → As a result.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"The (A) second test was (B) slightly (C) more (D) easier than the first.","o":["second","slightly","more","easier"],"k":3,"e":"No more with -er.","h":""}]}],"n":30}],"sc":{},"review":{"quiz":[{"l":["Unit Review — 50 questions. Questions 1–35: choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence. Questions 36–50: choose the ONE underlined part that is incorrect.","مراجعة الوحدة: خمسون سؤالًا؛ في الأسئلة من ١ إلى ٣٥ اختر الإجابة التي تكمل الجملة، وفي الأسئلة من ٣٦ إلى ٥٠ اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–35)"],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Never ______ so much rain in Riyadh in one day.","o":["have I seen","I have seen","I saw","did I saw"],"k":0,"e":"Never first → inversion.","h":"Never في البداية."},{"n":2,"s":"Not only ______ the race, but he also broke the record.","o":["he won","he did win","won he","did he win"],"k":3,"e":"Not only + did + subject.","h":"Not only + did."},{"n":3,"s":"No sooner had the bell rung ______ the students ran out.","o":["when","than","then","that"],"k":1,"e":"No sooner … than.","h":"No sooner مع than."},{"n":4,"s":"Under no circumstances ______ open this box.","o":["you should","you must","should you","do you must"],"k":2,"e":"Under no circumstances + modal + subject.","h":"القلب مع الفعل الناقص."},{"n":5,"s":"Only after the meeting ended ______ the truth.","o":["did we learn","we learned","we did learn","learned we"],"k":0,"e":"Invert the main clause after Only after.","h":"القلب بعد Only after."},{"n":6,"s":"It was my grandmother ______ taught me to read.","o":["which","who","where","whom she"],"k":1,"e":"Person focus → who.","h":"شخص who."},{"n":7,"s":"What we need ______ more time to practise.","o":["are","were","is","be"],"k":2,"e":"What … is.","h":"What … is."},{"n":8,"s":"I ______ tell you about the change; you just forgot.","o":["do","does","did","done"],"k":2,"e":"Emphatic past → did + base verb.","h":"التوكيد بـ did."},{"n":9,"s":"It is the nurses who ______ the hospital running at night.","o":["keep","keeps","is keeping","has kept"],"k":0,"e":"who refers to nurses (plural).","h":"التوافق مع nurses."},{"n":10,"s":"The children made the decorations ______.","o":["theirselves","themselves","himself","itself"],"k":1,"e":"Reflexive for they.","h":"themselves."},{"n":11,"s":"The box of old photos ______ in the cupboard.","o":["are","were","is","have been"],"k":2,"e":"Head noun box.","h":"الاسم الرئيس box."},{"n":12,"s":"Neither the students nor the teacher ______ the answer.","o":["know","knows","are knowing","have known"],"k":1,"e":"Nearest subject: the teacher.","h":"الأقرب teacher."},{"n":13,"s":"A number of new shops ______ opened in our area.","o":["has","is","was","have"],"k":3,"e":"a number of → plural.","h":"a number of جمع."},{"n":14,"s":"Economics ______ a popular subject at our university.","o":["is","are","were","have been"],"k":0,"e":"Economics is singular.","h":"Economics مفردة."},{"n":15,"s":"Each of the rooms ______ its own bathroom.","o":["has","have","are having","were having"],"k":0,"e":"each of → singular.","h":"each مفردة."},{"n":16,"s":"The ______ of the new airport will create thousands of jobs.","o":["construct","constructive","constructively","construction"],"k":3,"e":"After The → noun.","h":"بعد The اسم."},{"n":17,"s":"It is ______ to walk across the desert without water.","o":["impossible","unpossible","inpossible","dispossible"],"k":0,"e":"im- before p.","h":"im قبل p."},{"n":18,"s":"The children were ______ by the magic show.","o":["amazing","amaze","amazement","amazed"],"k":3,"e":"How people feel → -ed.","h":"شعور ed."},{"n":19,"s":"Pollution can ______ the growth of young plants.","o":["effect","effective","affect","affection"],"k":2,"e":"After can → verb affect.","h":"بعد can فعل."},{"n":20,"s":"The meal smelled ______.","o":["deliciously","deliciousness","delicacy","delicious"],"k":3,"e":"After smell (linking verb) → adjective.","h":"بعد smell صفة."},{"n":21,"s":"He likes hiking, camping and ______.","o":["fishing","to fish","fish","fishes"],"k":0,"e":"Parallel -ing.","h":"التوازي ing."},{"n":22,"s":"Could you tell me where ______?","o":["the nearest mosque is","is the nearest mosque","the nearest mosque does","does the nearest mosque"],"k":0,"e":"Embedded question → statement order.","h":"ترتيب الخبر."},{"n":23,"s":"She bought a ______ dress for the wedding.","o":["blue long beautiful","long beautiful blue","beautiful blue long","beautiful long blue"],"k":3,"e":"opinion → size → colour.","h":"الرأي ثم الحجم ثم اللون."},{"n":24,"s":"I'm not sure ______ the museum opens on Saturdays.","o":["if","that","does","what"],"k":0,"e":"Embedded yes / no → if.","h":"if."},{"n":25,"s":"The population of Riyadh is larger than ______ of Jeddah.","o":["those","it","this","that"],"k":3,"e":"Compare population with population → that of.","h":"that of."},{"n":26,"s":"The success of the project depends ______ good planning.","o":["of","on","from","at"],"k":1,"e":"depend on.","h":"depend on."},{"n":27,"s":"Many students ______ part in the science fair.","o":["made","did","took","had"],"k":2,"e":"take part in.","h":"take part in."},{"n":28,"s":"She is very proud ______ her son's achievements.","o":["with","of","for","about"],"k":1,"e":"proud of.","h":"proud of."},{"n":29,"s":"Scientists are ______ research on new medicines.","o":["making","taking","doing","having"],"k":2,"e":"do research.","h":"do research."},{"n":30,"s":"Our city is different ______ the city where I grew up.","o":["of","than of","from","with"],"k":2,"e":"different from.","h":"different from."},{"n":31,"s":"The harder you train, ______ you will play.","o":["better","the better","the best","more better"],"k":1,"e":"The … the + comparative.","h":"تركيب the … the."},{"n":32,"s":"The new phone is ______ faster than the old one.","o":["considerably","very","too","so"],"k":0,"e":"considerably + comparative.","h":"considerably مع المقارنة."},{"n":33,"s":"Ahmed enjoys science, ______ his sister prefers literature.","o":["moreover","therefore","nevertheless","whereas"],"k":3,"e":"Contrast within a sentence → whereas.","h":"whereas."},{"n":34,"s":"The road was closed. ______, we arrived on time.","o":["Whereas","Because","Nevertheless","Moreover"],"k":2,"e":"Surprising contrast in a new sentence.","h":"Nevertheless."},{"n":35,"s":"The new park is three times ______ the old one.","o":["as large as","larger as","as larger than","more large"],"k":0,"e":"three times as … as.","h":"المضاعفة."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 36–50)"],"q":[{"n":36,"s":"(A) Rarely (B) I have (C) seen such a (D) crowded market.","o":["Rarely","I have","seen","crowded"],"k":1,"e":"Rarely first → have I.","h":""},{"n":37,"s":"Hardly (A) had we (B) started the (C) picnic (D) than it began to rain.","o":["had","started","picnic","than"],"k":3,"e":"Hardly … when.","h":""},{"n":38,"s":"(A) What I want are a (B) quiet room (C) to (D) study in.","o":["What I want are","quiet","to","study"],"k":0,"e":"What … is.","h":""},{"n":39,"s":"It (A) was in (B) Madinah (C) where my father (D) was born.","o":["was","Madinah","where","was"],"k":2,"e":"It was + place + that.","h":""},{"n":40,"s":"(A) Twenty minutes (B) are not (C) enough to finish (D) this task.","o":["Twenty","are","enough","this"],"k":1,"e":"Amount of time → singular.","h":""},{"n":41,"s":"The (A) results of the (B) survey (C) shows that most people (D) prefer public transport.","o":["results","survey","shows","prefer"],"k":2,"e":"Head noun results (plural) → show.","h":""},{"n":42,"s":"The new rules had a (A) positive (B) affect on (C) student (D) behaviour.","o":["positive","affect","student","behaviour"],"k":1,"e":"After a positive → noun effect.","h":""},{"n":43,"s":"He (A) speaks English (B) fluent and (C) writes it (D) well.","o":["speaks","fluent","writes","well"],"k":1,"e":"Describes speaks → adverb fluently.","h":""},{"n":44,"s":"The (A) storm caused (B) serious (C) destroy to (D) many houses.","o":["storm","serious","destroy","many"],"k":2,"e":"After serious → noun destruction.","h":""},{"n":45,"s":"She (A) likes (B) painting, (C) reading and (D) to cook.","o":["likes","painting","reading","to cook"],"k":3,"e":"Parallel -ing.","h":""},{"n":46,"s":"Do you (A) know (B) why (C) is the shop (D) closed?","o":["know","why","is the shop","closed"],"k":2,"e":"Embedded question → statement order.","h":""},{"n":47,"s":"We (A) discussed (B) about the (C) problem (D) for an hour.","o":["discussed","about","problem","for"],"k":1,"e":"discuss takes no preposition.","h":""},{"n":48,"s":"The (A) more you practise, (B) the (C) more confident you (D) are become.","o":["more","the","more confident","are become"],"k":3,"e":"Verb form: you become.","h":""},{"n":49,"s":"Please (A) pay (B) more (C) attention (D) at the instructions.","o":["pay","more","attention","at"],"k":3,"e":"pay attention to.","h":""},{"n":50,"s":"The new (A) hall is (B) very (C) larger than (D) the old one.","o":["hall","very","larger","the"],"k":1,"e":"No very with comparatives.","h":""}]}],"n":50}};
